\item \textbf{Publication strategy}, including ACS journals, the CAPES agreement, and high-impact alternatives;
\item \textbf{\code{--make\_images} (V39)}: it was found that, even without \code{--video}, the program unconditionally generated 4--5 summary PNG images per run. This cost is negligible in large arrays, but dominant in small arrays used for sweeps. The new parameter suppresses all image generation while preserving data CSVs, with a measured speedup of $\sim 3\times$ in small runs (2.03~s $\to$ 0.65~s for an $8\times8$ array);
\item \textbf{Campaign infrastructure}: the scripts \code{damping\_sweep.py} (orchestration of damping~$\times$~\emph{seed}~$\times$~geometry sweeps, calling the simulator programmatically) and \code{damping\_sweep\_analysis.py} (full statistical analysis), both validated end to end (Section~\ref{sec:campaign});
\item \textbf{Performance optimizations implemented (04/07)}: the precomputed dipolar tensor (\textbf{V40}) and campaign parallelization with incremental \emph{manifest} and resume support (\code{damping\_sweep} V02). Details and measurements are in Section~\ref{sec:improvements}. The measured V40 speedup is \textbf{35--45$\times$} per run, reducing the full campaign from $\sim$7--8~h to $\sim$15~min on a single core;
